[38;2;248;248;242m         Tries to reinstate not only the working tree’s changes, but also the index’s ones. However, this can fail, when you have conflicts (which are stored in the index, where you therefore can no longer apply the changes as they were originally).[0m

[38;2;248;248;242m     [0m[38;2;166;226;46m--label-ours[0m[38;2;249;38;114m=[0m[38;2;253;151;31m<label>[0m[38;2;248;248;242m, [0m[38;2;166;226;46m--label-theirs[0m[38;2;249;38;114m=[0m[38;2;253;151;31m<label>[0m[38;2;248;248;242m, [0m[38;2;166;226;46m--label-base[0m[38;2;249;38;114m=[0m[38;2;253;151;31m<label>[0m
[38;2;248;248;242m         These options are only valid for the apply command.[0m

[38;2;248;248;242m         Use the given labels in conflict markers instead of the default "Updated upstream", "Stashed changes", and "Stash base".  [0m[38;2;166;226;46m--label-base[0m[38;2;248;248;242m only has an effect with merge.conflictStyle=diff3.[0m

[38;2;248;248;242m     [0m[38;2;166;226;46m-k[0m[38;2;248;248;242m, [0m[38;2;166;226;46m--keep-index[0m[38;2;248;248;242m, [0m[38;2;166;226;46m--no-keep-index[0m
[38;2;248;248;242m         This option is only valid for push and save commands.[0m

[38;2;248;248;242m         All changes already added to the index are left intact.[0m

